Confirm the result. The agent returns your open issues, just as it did in the previous lab, but what happened underneath is different. The deployed agent held no token. When your query arrived, the ADK used the agent's SPIFFE identity to fetch the API key from the auth provider, attached it as the Authorization header, and called the GitHub MCP server. The credential lived in the auth manager the whole time and was read just in time for the call.

Note: This also means access is now governed by IAM. If you removed the binding you granted above, this same request would fail with a permission error instead of returning data, which confirms the secret is no longer baked into the agent.
