Task 4. Create the Salesforce 2LO auth provider
In this task, you create the second auth provider, this time for Salesforce. The Salesforce agent authenticates to the Salesforce REST/SOSL API with an app-only client-credentials grant. The app acts as itself, with no signed-in user, so the right auth provider is 2-legged OAuth (2LO). You store the Connected App consumer key, secret, and token endpoint in the auth provider, and the auth manager performs the grant and refreshes the token for you.

Set your Salesforce values from the previous lab. SF_DOMAIN is your org's My Domain host. The consumer key and secret come from the Connected App's client-credentials flow.

