Understand how the token reaches the tool
Removing the hardcoded secret changed two files: In tools.py you registered the auth provider, declared an AuthConfig that names the 2LO auth provider, and wrapped the tool in an AuthenticatedFunctionTool; the token now comes from an injected credential instead of client.authenticate(). In agent.py you built the client with no credentials (only the My Domain) and passed it to build_search_salesforce. Because the Salesforce search is a plain REST call from your own function, the ADK can hand the credential straight to your code — there is no header plumbing.

Here is how the access token reaches Salesforce on each tool call:

During import: tools.py runs CredentialManager.register_auth_provider(GcpAuthProvider()) and builds salesforce_auth_config, which names your 2LO auth provider.
Wiring: agent.py creates a credential-free SalesforceClient(domain=...) and calls build_search_salesforce(client). The factory returns an AuthenticatedFunctionTool that wraps search_salesforce, with client captured in the closure.
The model calls the tool with only query. The AuthenticatedFunctionTool intercepts the call and asks the ADK to resolve the auth provider, using the agent's own identity (its Cloud Run service account).
Auth Manager returns an AuthCredential holding a fresh, app-only access token. The ADK injects it as the credential argument — the model never sees it.
Your function reads the token with _extract_token(credential) and passes it to the client's search_files, which runs the SOSL query and downloads the top hits to build content snippets.
The client calls Salesforce with an Authorization: Bearer header, against the REST base derived from your My Domain, and returns the results. No consumer key or secret ever touched your code, and the token is refreshed for you.
Compare this to the GitHub agent, where the tool is a remote MCP server and you had to attach the token yourself with a header_provider. It is the same auth provider mechanism with two delivery styles: an argument for function tools, a header for MCP tools.

Salesforce 2LO flow: Auth Manager returns a refreshed token, then the tool function calls the Salesforce REST/SOSL API

