export SF_URL=$(gcloud run services describe salesforce-agent --region ${REGION} --format='value(status.url)')
agents-cli run --url ${SF_URL} --mode a2a "Search for any architecture decision records about timeouts."
Copied!
Troubleshooting: If the agent returns an empty answer, the token exchange with Salesforce likely failed. Auth Manager resolves the credential before your tool function runs, so a bad auth provider value surfaces as an error rather than the tool's own message. Check the Cloud Run logs for CONNECTOR_AUTH_TOKEN_EXCHANGE_ERROR and confirm the auth provider's client id, secret, and token endpoint (and that the Connected App's client-credentials run-as user can read the files).
Confirm the result. The agent returns matching documents from Salesforce Files. As with the GitHub agent, the deployed Salesforce agent holds no Salesforce credentials. The ADK used the Cloud Run service account to fetch a fresh access token from the 2LO auth provider and called the Salesforce API with it. Both specialists now authenticate to their external tools through the auth manager, with no secrets in their code.

