In this lab, you removed hardcoded tool secrets from two agents and put them behind Agent Identity Auth Manager. You created an API-key auth provider for the GitHub MCP server and a 2-legged OAuth provider for Salesforce, refactored each agent to resolve its credential through the ADK, and authorized each agent's identity to use its auth provider: a SPIFFE principal for the Agent Runtime agent and a service account for the Cloud Run agent. Both credentials now live in one governed place, where you can rotate or revoke them without editing or redeploying an agent.

